      "writtenOn": "2017-04-03T08:54:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: is this a behaviour change? Previously, a specifier of \"\" would have been treated as equal to a null specifier. What do we do now?\n\nIf this is in fact a behaviour change, can/should we avoid it by ensuring that if the user passes in \"\", then we silently set the specifier to null?\n\nI don\u0027t think that would be a change in app-visible behaviour because getNetworkSpecifier() is @hide.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 627,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 627,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "ce49b2d880a5e25f90c1d5ad77d62f5d3fc68590",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
